im]\n    [#D7D7AF]coordination: make every Gmail read latch auth aborts and give-ups in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]one injectable coordinator, turn search and preparation failures into a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]body-free failure state without discarding adoption or recovery, account[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the -r budget only for waits, and fix the report's membership snapshot [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and warnings, with unit tests for each.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Host-local, idempotent commit and journal recovery[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]recovery[dim] · [dim][/dim]after coordination[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]recovery: move the sync recovery evidence to host-local state, make its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]replay idempotent per event and ownership-checked per path, stop writing[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]auxiliary files on runs that save no note, keep in-flight filings from [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]being filed twice, and add the temporary-Git-vault recovery tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end acceptance matrix, alias parity, and lint [/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]scaffolding[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]acceptance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after recovery[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]acceptance: add the missing tests/gmail_sync.rs composition coverage, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]including byte-identical sync versus pull in separate fixed-time [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fixtures, and remove the stale dead_code allowances left from the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]command phase.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Sync documentation, help, and generated CLI reference[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after acceptance[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n